(ned ROTARY FACING -- stock prep. Skim a bar down to a target diameter.)
(Operator 2026-08-12: tool number, starting D, end D, begin and end Y.)

(ALWAYS AT G55 X0. The tool sits on the rotary centreline plane, so its tip)
(contacts the crown and nothing else. Diameter therefore comes straight from)
(Z: tip at Z = D/2 IS diameter D. No radial compensation, and none is)
(wanted -- X is not an input and is never commanded.)

(THE COMPENSATION IS IN Y, BECAUSE THE Y VALUES ARE EDGES. The tool bottom is)
(a disc: sweeping its CENTRE from y1 to y2 actually machines y1-R to y2+R. To)
(finish exactly between the two edges the operator gave, the centre runs)
(y1+R to y2-R. A cut narrower than the tool is refused rather than fudged.)

(Y FEED IS COMPUTED, NOT ACCEPTED. One turn of B advances Y by one pitch, so)
(Y speed and B speed are the same fact twice. B tops out at 30 deg/s, which)
(caps Y at pitch * 30 / 360 * 60 mm/min -- 63 mm/min for a 12.7 tool at full)
(pitch. Asking for more just means LinuxCNC clamps B and the real feed is)
(whatever it was always going to be; better to say so than to pretend.)
(Chip load will replace this later - operator: we will refactor.)

(D_START IS A PROMISE, NOT A MEASUREMENT. The first pass is taken at)
(D_START - DOC on the assumption nothing sticks out past D_START. Nothing)
(here can see the stock, so an optimistic number buries the tool on move one.)
o<rotary_face> sub
  #<rf_tool>   = #1 (=0 tool number - required)
  #<rf_dstart> = #2 (=0 stock diameter now mm - required)
  #<rf_dend>   = #3 (=0 target diameter mm - required)
  #<rf_y1>     = #4 (=0 Y begin - an EDGE of the cut)
  #<rf_y2>     = #5 (=0 Y end - an EDGE of the cut)
  #<rf_doc>    = #6 (=1.0 radial depth per pass mm)
  #<rf_rpm>    = #7 (=9000 spindle rpm)
  #<rf_step>   = #8 (=0.5 pitch as a fraction of tool diameter)
  #<rf_bmax>   = #9 (=30.0 B max deg/s - JOINT_6 MAX_VELOCITY)
  o1 if [#<rf_doc> LE 0]
    #<rf_doc> = 1.0
  o1 endif
  o2 if [#<rf_rpm> LE 0]
    #<rf_rpm> = 9000
  o2 endif
  o3 if [#<rf_step> LE 0]
    #<rf_step> = 0.5
  o3 endif
  o4 if [#<rf_bmax> LE 0]
    #<rf_bmax> = 30.0
  o4 endif
  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: switch to MM first)
  o10 endif
  o11 if [#<rf_tool> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: no tool number given)
  o11 endif
  o12 if [#<rf_dstart> LE 0 OR #<rf_dend> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: both start and end diameter are required)
  o12 endif
  o13 if [#<rf_dend> GE #<rf_dstart>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: end diameter must be SMALLER than the start diameter)
  o13 endif
  o14 if [#<rf_y2> LE #<rf_y1>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: Y end must be greater than Y begin)
  o14 endif

  T#<rf_tool> M6
  G43
  o20 if [#5400 NE #<rf_tool>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: the spindle is not holding the tool that was asked for)
  o20 endif
  #<tdia> = #5410
  o21 if [#<tdia> LE 0]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: that tool has no diameter in the table)
  o21 endif
  #<trad> = [#<tdia> / 2.0]

  (EDGE COMPENSATION)
  #<ya> = [#<rf_y1> + #<trad>]
  #<yb> = [#<rf_y2> - #<trad>]
  o22 if [#<yb> LE #<ya>]
    (abort, ROTARY FACE: that span is narrower than the tool - nothing to sweep)
  o22 endif

  (PITCH AND THE FEED IT IMPLIES)
  #<pitch> = [#<tdia> * #<rf_step>]
  #<feed>  = [#<pitch> * #<rf_bmax> * 60.0 / 360.0]
  #<zsafe> = [[#<rf_dstart> / 2.0] + 10.0]
  (PRINT, ROTARY FACE: T#<rf_tool> dia #<tdia>, pitch #<pitch> mm/rev, Y feed #<feed> mm/min at B #<rf_bmax> deg/s)
  (PRINT, ROTARY FACE: sweeping Y #<ya> to #<yb> - tool centre, edges at #<rf_y1> and #<rf_y2>)

  G90
  G1 G53 Z0 F2000
  M3 S#<rf_rpm>
  G0 Z[#<zsafe>]
  G0 Y[#<ya>]
  G0 B0

  #<d> = #<rf_dstart>
  #<pass> = 0
  o100 while [#<d> GT #<rf_dend>]
    #<d> = [#<d> - #<rf_doc>]
    o101 if [#<d> LT #<rf_dend>]
      #<d> = #<rf_dend>
    o101 endif
    #<pass> = [#<pass> + 1]
    #<z> = [#<d> / 2.0]
    (PRINT, ROTARY FACE: pass #<pass> to diameter #<d>, Z #<z>)
    G0 Y[#<ya>]
    G0 Z[#<z> + 2.0]
    G1 Z[#<z>] F[#<feed>]
    (ONE STEP PER 10 DEG OF B: fine enough that the helix is not faceted,)
    (coarse enough that a 100 mm pass is not 3600 blocks.)
    #<len>   = [#<yb> - #<ya>]
    #<revs>  = [#<len> / #<pitch>]
    #<steps> = [FIX[#<revs> * 36.0] + 1]
    #<dy>    = [#<len> / #<steps>]
    #<db>    = [#<revs> * 360.0 / #<steps>]
    #<i>     = 0
    #<yy>    = #<ya>
    #<bb>    = 0
    o110 while [#<i> LT #<steps>]
      #<yy> = [#<yy> + #<dy>]
      #<bb> = [#<bb> + #<db>]
      G1 Y[#<yy>] B[#<bb>] F[#<feed>]
      #<i> = [#<i> + 1]
    o110 endwhile
    G0 Z[#<zsafe>]
  o100 endwhile

  G0 G53 Z0
  M5
  (PRINT, ROTARY FACE DONE: #<pass> passes, stock now #<rf_dend> mm across the sweep.)
o<rotary_face> endsub
M2 (end program)
